2026-01-05 15:29:39,586 - INCOMING FROM AI (RAW): ''<think>\nI need to create a Python script that:\n1. Asks the user for an interval in minutes.\n2. Uses that interval to launch system notifications in Android Termux environment.\n\nIn Termux, we can use the `termux-notification` command to show notifications. The script should:\n- Prompt for interval input (float or integer).\n- Convert minutes to seconds (since sleep typically uses seconds).\n- Run in a loop, showing a notification at each interval.\n\nI\'ll create a script with error handling and clear instructions. First, I should check if the required Termux API is available, but I\'ll assume it\'s installed. I\'ll write the script to a file, e.g., `interval_notifier.py`.\n\nLet me write the script content.\n</think>\n{\n  "type": "write_file",\n  "path": "interval_notifier.py",\n  "content": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\"\\"\\"\\nInterval Notifier for Android Termux\\nThis script asks for an interval in minutes and shows a system notification\\nat that interval repeatedly.\\n\\"\\"\\"\\n\\nimport subprocess\\nimport time\\nimport sys\\n\\ndef show_notification(title=\\"Interval Notifier\\", message=\\"Time\'s up!\\"):\\n    \\"\\"\\"Show a system notification using termux-notification.\\"\\"\\"\\n    try:\\n        subprocess.run([\\n            \'termux-notification\',\\n            \'--title\', title,\\n            \'--content\', message,\\n            \'--sound\'  # Optional: add sound\\n        ], check=True)\\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\\n        print(f\\"Failed to show notification: {e}\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n    except FileNotFoundError:\\n        print(\\"Error: \'termux-notification\' command not found. Ensure Termux:API is installed.\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        print(\\"Install via: pkg install termux-api\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        sys.exit(1)\\n\\ndef main():\\n    print(\\"=== Interval Notifier for Termux ===\\")\\n    print(\\"This script will show a notification at you